- I did not verify behavior for non-`Error` throws in third-party middleware in the wild (e.g., whether any bundled middleware in `src/middleware/*` deliberately throws non-Error values) — only reasoned from `compose.ts`'s literal `instanceof Error` check.
- I did not trace `c.error` usage elsewhere in the codebase (e.g., whether other built-in middleware reads `context.error` after `next()`) beyond confirming it's set in `compose.ts`.

